<title>CANADA: Canada dollar weaker ahead of Greenspan testimony.</title>
<headline>Canada dollar weaker ahead of Greenspan testimony.</headline>
<text>
<p>FORECAST RANGE   1.3715/1.3755	   ASIAN CLOSE     1.3730</p>
<p>RESISTANCE 1.3653   SUPPORT 1.3803     HI 1.3743   LO  1.3720</p>
<p>CANADA OPEN  1.3728/33    HI 1.3746    EUROPE OPEN     1.3714</p>
<p>PREV CLOSE   1.3744/49    LO 1.3726    HI 1.3728   LO  1.3714</p>
<p>---------------------MARKET COMMENT--------------------------</p>
<p>* Canada's dollar was slightly weaker at C$1.3740 (US$0.7278) in light midday trading on Monday as investors sold short positions ahead of U.S. Federal Chairman Alan Greenspan's Humphrey-Hawkins testimony, dealers said. * They said the release of retail sales data showing a 0.5 percent increase in May failed to move the Canada dollar.</p>
